),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`what-is-a-task%3F`,children:`What is a task?`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Tasks are defined as decorated Python functions. Above, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`explain_tasks`}),` is an instance of a task.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Tasks are cache-able and retryable units of work that are easy to execute concurrently, in parallel, and/or with `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/v3/advanced/transactions`,children:`transactional semantics`}),`.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Like flows, tasks are free to call other tasks or flows, there is no required nesting pattern.`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Generally, tasks behave like normal Python functions, but they have some additional capabilities:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsx(_components.li,{children:`Metadata about task runs, such as run time and final state, is automatically tracked`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Each `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/v3/concepts/states/`,children:`state`}),` the task enters is recorded, enabling observability and state-based logic`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/v3/how-to-guides/workflows/run-work-concurrently#handling-futures`,children:`Futures`}),` from upstream tasks are automatically resolved by downstream tasks`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/v3/how-to-guides/workflows/retries`,children:`Retries`}),` can be performed on failure, with configurable delay and retry limits`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/v3/how-to-guides/workflows/cache-workflow-steps`,children:`Caching`}),` enables result reuse across workflow executions`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/v3/how-to-guides/workflows/run-work-concurrently`,children:`Concurrency`}),` via `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.submit()`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.map()`}),` allow concurr